  <div class="meetup-colonne">

    <section class="meetup-hero" aria-labelledby="meetup-titre">
      <h1 id="meetup-titre">Antoine Olivier</h1>
      <p class="meetup-chapo"><strong>Independent researcher.</strong> I do scientific research with AI agents, I’m launching DiscoverIA and I develop the AZERTY Global keyboard layout.</p>
      <div class="meetup-hero-actions meetup-actions">
        <a class="meetup-btn" href="mailto:{{ mail }}">Email me</a>
        <a class="meetup-btn meetup-btn--secondaire" href="#kepler-circle">Co-found Kepler Circle</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="discoveria" class="meetup-section meetup-carte" aria-labelledby="discoveria-titre">
      <h2 id="discoveria-titre">DiscoverIA</h2>
      <p class="meetup-prose">DiscoverIA is a public site that tracks scientific and technological advances made by humans with AI. Each advance carries a sourced, dated status, and the history of that status stays visible.</p>
      <ul class="meetup-faits">
        <li><strong>Understand:</strong> each advance is explained simply, with its sources and dates.</li>
        <li><strong>Check:</strong> where a result stands, who confirmed it, what has changed since it was announced.</li>
        <li><strong>Take part:</strong> reproduce a result yourself, or report an advance that is missing.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="meetup-actions">
        <a class="meetup-btn" href="https://discoveria.ai/en/" rel="noopener">Open discoveria.ai</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="recherche" class="meetup-section" aria-labelledby="recherche-titre">
      <h2 id="recherche-titre">My research with AI agents</h2>
      <p class="meetup-prose">Since late September 2026, I have been running a research lab of AI agents at home. They work on open problems in mathematics, astronomy and physics.</p>
      <p class="meetup-prose">The lab works in five steps:</p>
      <ol class="meetup-etapes">
        <li>the idea;</li>
        <li>the attack;</li>
        <li>hostile review;</li>
        <li>certified computation;</li>
        <li>the computer-verified proof.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="meetup-prose">Each result goes through some or all of these steps. Only some of them have a computer-verified proof.</p>

      <div class="meetup-registre">
        <p class="meetup-registre-tete" aria-hidden="true"><span>Result</span><span>Status, source and date</span></p>
        <ul class="meetup-registre-liste">
          <li class="meetup-entree">
            <div>
              <h3>Error-correcting codes</h3>
              <p>An error-correcting code protects a message against transmission errors. My agents found codes that protect more messages than the best ones known until then.</p>
            </div>
            <p class="meetup-statut"><strong>12&nbsp;records in my name</strong> Andries Brouwer’s reference table, read on 25&nbsp;October 2026. Codes published on Zenodo.</p>
          </li>
          <li class="meetup-entree">
            <div>
              <h3>Kissing number in 37&nbsp;dimensions</h3>
              <p>How many balls can touch another one? In 3&nbsp;dimensions, the answer is 12. In a 37‑dimensional space, my agents found an arrangement of 500,008&nbsp;balls.</p>
            </div>
            <p class="meetup-statut"><strong>Record of 22&nbsp;October 2026, since beaten</strong> By another researcher. Henry Cohn’s table (MIT).</p>
          </li>
          <li class="meetup-entree">
            <div>
              <h3>Jammed balls in 5&nbsp;dimensions</h3>
              <p>In a 5‑dimensional space, two arrangements of 40&nbsp;balls are jammed: no ball can move. They were found on 10&nbsp;October 2026 and verified by computer.</p>
            </div>
            <p class="meetup-statut"><strong>Found independently</strong> Matthew Self published it first, independently, on 15&nbsp;October 2026.</p>
          </li>
          <li class="meetup-entree">
            <div>
              <h3>Terence Tao’s challenge</h3>
              <p>I replayed another participant’s computer-verified proof and linked it to the official statement of the challenge.</p>
            </div>
            <p class="meetup-statut"><strong>Verification</strong> 23&nbsp;October 2026, on Terence Tao’s blog.</p>
          </li>
          <li class="meetup-entree">
            <div>
              <h3>Exoplanets</h3>
              <p>While rechecking candidate exoplanets flagged by another researcher’s program, I found a bug in that program. The author fixed it and credits me.</p>
            </div>
            <p class="meetup-statut"><strong>Bug fixed</strong> Reported on GitHub.</p>
          </li>
          <li class="meetup-entree">
            <div>
              <h3>Gravitational waves</h3>
              <p>I am preparing a comment on a paper, based on public data.</p>
            </div>
            <p class="meetup-statut"><strong>In preparation</strong></p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="kepler-circle" class="meetup-section meetup-appel"aria-labelledby="kepler-titre">
      <h2 id="kepler-titre">Founding Kepler Circle</h2>
      <p class="meetup-prose">Kepler Circle will be a non-profit research association under French law (loi&nbsp;1901). It will publish these results with their checks and the scripts to reproduce them. Its registration is under way.</p>
      <p class="meetup-prose">An association needs at least two founders. I am looking for the person who will found it with me. If you are interested, email me.</p>
      <div class="meetup-actions">
        <a class="meetup-btn" href="mailto:{{ mail }}?subject=Kepler%20Circle">Email me about Kepler Circle</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="financer" class="meetup-section meetup-appel"aria-labelledby="financer-titre">
      <h2 id="financer-titre">Funding my research</h2>
      <p class="meetup-prose">I am looking for funders for my research and my projects: research, open source and tools for the French language.</p>
      <div class="meetup-actions">
        <a class="meetup-btn" href="mailto:{{ mail }}?subject=Funding">Email me about funding</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="azerty-global" class="meetup-section" aria-labelledby="azerty-titre">
      <h2 id="azerty-titre">The AZERTY Global keyboard layout</h2>
      <p class="meetup-prose">An improved AZERTY, free and open source: accented capitals É È Ç À, French quotation marks «&nbsp;», programming symbols within easy reach. Windows, macOS and Linux.</p>
      <p class="meetup-prose">I have been running AZERTY Global since 2017, now with the AMCF association, which I chair.</p>
      <div class="meetup-actions">
        <a class="meetup-btn" href="/en/download">Download AZERTY Global</a>
        <a class="meetup-btn meetup-btn--secondaire" href="/bienvenue">Try it online</a>
      </div>
    </section>

